 setjmp:        , name,
C===========================================================
C setjmp(env) - record the current frame, return address and
C   display registers.
C   In:  ACC  = env (pointer to a six-word jmp_buf).
C   env[0] will be packed (caller frame << 15) | setjmp-return-addr,
C   matching what longjmp.madlen expects: low 15 bits = address
C   to jump back to, high part = caller's frame pointer (M7).
C   env[1] through env[5] hold M2 through M6, the display
C   registers C/2..C/6 save in every frame and C/E restores; a
C   longjmp does not pass through C/E, so it restores them from
C   here instead.  They are written by pointing the stack at
C   env[1] and pushing, the caller's M15 parked in M14 meanwhile.
C   Out: ACC := 0   (the "first" return value of setjmp).
C===========================================================
                , ntr , 7      . ABI requirement
            15  , mtj , 14     . M14 := M15, the caller's stack pointer
                , ati , 15     . M15 := env (consume the arg pointer)
                , ita , 13     . ACC := M13 (return address)
            15  , atx ,        . env[0] := return address (low 15 bits)
C   Addressed through M15 at offset zero, a read pops and a write
C   pushes, so the AOX below takes env[0] back and the ITS that
C   stores it again leaves M15 addressing env[1], which is where
C   the display run continues.
                , ita , 7      . ACC := M7 (caller's frame pointer)
                , asn , 64-15  . left-shift 15 (frame -> high part)
            15  , aox ,        . ACC := (frame << 15) | env[0]
                , its , 2      . env[0] := packed value; ACC := M2
                , its , 3      . env[1] := M2; ACC := M3
                , its , 4      . env[2] := M3; ACC := M4
                , its , 5      . env[3] := M4; ACC := M5
                , its , 6      . env[4] := M5; ACC := M6
            15  , atx ,        . env[5] := M6
            14  , mtj , 15     . M15 := the caller's stack pointer again
                , xta ,        . ACC := 0 (setjmp's first-time return)
            13  , uj  ,        . return via M13
                , end ,
